<PolicyLayout title="Copyright and Takedown Policy">
  <p>Uploaders keep their copyright and grant the limited service licence in the <a class="text-link" href="/policies/terms/">Terms of Service</a>. Public availability does not give other visitors permission to reuse a photo. The source-code licence does not cover user photos.</p>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Report an infringement</h2><p class="mt-3">Use the report control on a published photo or email the monitored contact below. For a copyright notice, please provide:</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6"><li>Your name and a contact email, and whether you are the rights holder or an authorised representative.</li><li>A description of the copyrighted work and a link or other evidence that identifies it.</li><li>The exact VeloGroupsets photo or page URL you want reviewed.</li><li>Why you believe the use is unauthorised, and a good-faith statement that your information is accurate and you are entitled to make the request.</li><li>Your typed name or other appropriate signature.</li></ul><p class="mt-3">Do not send passwords, identity documents or unnecessary personal information with an initial notice. We may ask for proportionate clarification if needed.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What happens next</h2><p class="mt-3">We review reports, may hide the image while investigating, and may remove it, contact the uploader or restrict an account. Where appropriate, we may share the substance of a claim with the uploader so they can respond, while limiting unnecessary disclosure of contact information. Applicable legal requirements take precedence over this general process.</p><p class="mt-3">Uploaders can respond with evidence of ownership, permission or another lawful basis, or explain why a claim identifies the wrong work. We do not automatically restore disputed content after a fixed period. Contact the operator to request a review of a decision.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Privacy, safety and other takedowns</h2><p class="mt-3">You can also report exposure of personal information, harassment or other prohibited content without making a copyright claim. Identify the URL and the concern. Suspected illegal material should be reported by URL only; do not download it or send a copy. Appropriate authorities may also need to be notified.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Removal and preservation</h2><p class="mt-3">Once removed, a photo is hidden from the public gallery and site image endpoint. We delete its public storage copy and request CDN cache removal, with retries if the cache service is unavailable. Some downloaded or independently cached copies may remain outside our control. We may preserve a restricted private copy and records where needed for a legal obligation or investigation.</p></section>
</PolicyLayout>
